    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="0381" n="283" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg283"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.512/1053</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Consul at Swatow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Berger</hi>)<anchor n="17" xml:id="d353-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-31">July 31, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Legation has received your despatch of
                    June 20, 1930,<anchor n="18" xml:id="d353-f2"/> inquiring whether you might
                    correctly protest against taxation in cases where there is no discrimination
                    against American goods.</p>
                <p>Provided that none of the commodities taxed have paid transit dues in lieu of
                    likin, and provided there is no discrimination against American goods, you
                    should refrain from any protest against the taxation mentioned. The Department
                    has held that, by accepting transit dues and issuing a transit pass which
                    purports to free the goods covered from all inland taxation en route, the
                    Chinese Government has entered into a contract and that attempts to levy likin
                    and inland taxes on goods covered by transit pass may properly be protested
                    against.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mahlon F.
                            Perkins</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Legation</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d353-f1" n="17" type="source" xml:id="d353-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to the Department by the Minister in China in his despatch No.
                    363, July 31, 1930; received September 10.</p>
            </note>
